          "is_primary": false
        },
        {
          "full_name": "NALU",
          "script": "Latn",
          "is_primary": false
        }
      ],
      "remarks": "CDe.001 Other information: ADF founder and leader, Jamil Mukulu (CDi.015), was arrested in Dar es Salaam, Tanzania in April 2015. He was subsequently extradited to Kampala, Uganda in July 2015. As of June 2016, Mukulu is reportedly being held in a police detention cell awaiting his trial. Seka Baluku (CDi.036) succeeded Jamil Mukulu (CDi.015) as the overall leader of the ADF. As highlighted in several reports from the Group of Experts on the DRC (S/2015/19, S/2015/797, S/2016/1102, S/2017/672, S/2018/531, S/2019/469, S/2019/974, S/2020/482), the ADF, including under Seka Baluku’s leadership, continued to commit the repeated targeting, killing and maiming, rape and other sexual violence, abduction of civilians, including children, as well as attacks on villages and health facilities, in particular in Mamove, Beni territory, on 12 and 24 February 2019, and Mantumbi, Beni territory, on 5 December 2019 and 30 January 2020, as well as the continuous recruitment and use of children during attacks and for forced labour in Beni territory in the DRC since at least 2015.; Listing: Listed by 1533 Committee on: 30 June 2014 (amended on 19 October 2016, 19 August 2020)",
      "addresses": [
        {
          "street": "North Kivu Province, Democratic Republic of the Congo",
          "country": "Democratic Republic of the Congo"
        }
      ]
    },
